exports[`rhachet roles boot — the budget gate, on a role coordinate given: [case4] a LINKED role whose spec exceeds its own budget when: [t2] roles cost --all, over the same real link then: the roster renders as snapshotted — on STDOUT: stdout-cost-all-linked 1`] = `
"🧢 1 boot spec — 1 budgeted, 1 over budget
   ├─ 506 / 20 tokens (2530%)  .agent/repo=linked-repo/role=lodger/boot.yml (linked) 🟡
   │
   └─ swept
      ├─ .agent/repo=*/role=*/boot.yml
      ├─ .behavior/*/boot.yml
      ├─ .route/*/boot.yml
      └─ src/domain.roles/*/boot.yml

   .note = a spec outside these paths is not swept. name it directly to cost it —
           \`roles cost --what <path>\`.

   .note = a \`(linked)\` spec is owned by another repo — not yours to trim. its budget is
           that repo's to raise, so \`roles boot\` warns on it rather than halts. upgrade
           the package, or raise it upstream. (1 of 1 here)

"
`;

